From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:21:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: avd: do not stop a stream for a frame
 the codec refused

A stream is stopped at its first frame that fails in hardware, with an
error-level message. A frame whose prepare() or run() fails never reached
the hardware (both only build the instruction program), yet it counted
the same, so one picture the codec could not describe ended the stream
and every later frame of it failed until streaming restarted.

Mark a refused whole picture refused: it still completes in error, but
it no longer counts as a hardware failure, stops the stream or prints.
A frame-based HEVC picture from Chromium ended the whole stream this
way. A refused part of a held picture (HOLD_CAPTURE) still stops the
stream, as before: that picture's CAPTURE buffer would otherwise come
back without those slices.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../platform/apple/avd/avd-queue-internal.h   |  1 +
 drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-queue.c  | 19 +++++++++++++++++--
 drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-queue.h  |  2 ++
 3 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-queue-internal.h b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-queue-internal.h
index c5b9c06836..19d0241e5f 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-queue-internal.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-queue-internal.h
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@ static inline int avd_slot_reserve(struct avd_frame *f, struct avd_ctx *ctx,
 	f->state = AVD_FRAME_RESERVED;
 	f->dep = AVD_DEP_NONE;
 	f->status = 0;
+	f->refused = false;
 	f->vp_done = false;
 	f->vp_retired = false;
 	f->prog_words = 0;
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-queue.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-queue.c
index 22e40b631a..f62daee59f 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-queue.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-queue.c
@@ -10,7 +10,11 @@
 #include "avd-queue-internal.h"
 
 #define AVD_FRAME_TIMEOUT msecs_to_jiffies(2000)
-/* A stream is stopped at its first frame that fails in hardware. */
+/*
+ * A stream is stopped at its first frame that fails in hardware. A whole
+ * picture the codec refused never reached it: it completes in error and the
+ * stream goes on.
+ */
 #define AVD_CTX_MAX_HW_ERRORS 1
 /* Never reset the decoder more often than this. */
 #define AVD_RECOVER_GAP_MS 20
@@ -78,6 +82,8 @@ static void avd_retire(struct avd_dev *avd)
 			state = f->status ? VB2_BUF_STATE_ERROR : VB2_BUF_STATE_DONE;
 			if (!f->status) {
 				ctx->hw_errors = 0;
+			} else if (f->refused) {
+				/* nothing reached the hardware */
 			} else if (++ctx->hw_errors >= AVD_CTX_MAX_HW_ERRORS && !ctx->broken) {
 				ctx->broken = true;
 				dev_err(avd->dev, "stream stopped after %u failed frames; restart streaming to retry\n",
@@ -476,8 +482,17 @@ static void avd_queue_submit_work(struct work_struct *work)
 		ret = ctx->coded_fmt_desc->ops->run(ctx);
 		avd->building = NULL;
 	}
-	if (ret)
+	if (ret) {
+		/*
+		 * prepare() and run() only build the program, so a refused whole
+		 * picture never reached the hardware. A refused part of a held
+		 * picture still stops the stream: its CAPTURE buffer would come
+		 * back without those slices.
+		 */
+		f->refused = !(f->src->flags & V4L2_BUF_FLAG_M2M_HOLD_CAPTURE_BUF) &&
+			     !f->dst->is_held;
 		goto fail;
+	}
 	ctx->next_dep = ops ? f->dep : AVD_DEP_PREV_DONE;
 	if ((ops && (f->src->flags & V4L2_BUF_FLAG_M2M_HOLD_CAPTURE_BUF)) ||
 	    (!ops && avd->compat_held)) {
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-queue.h b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-queue.h
index 038c4f9113..f83e452df2 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-queue.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-queue.h
@@ -33,6 +33,8 @@ struct avd_frame {
 	enum avd_frame_state state;
 	enum avd_frame_dep dep;
 	int status;			/* 0 or -EIO/-ETIMEDOUT from the backend */
+	/* The codec refused the frame before any of it reached the hardware. */
+	bool refused;
 
 	struct avd_ctx *ctx;
 	struct vb2_v4l2_buffer *src;	/* OUTPUT, held until retire */
-- 
2.43.0

